      "raw_text": "To solve this problem, we need to determine the total capacity of the trays and compare it to the number of eggs Jaime has.\n\n**Step 1: Calculate the total number of eggs the trays can hold.**\nEach tray holds 24 eggs, and Jaime has 2 trays.\n$$ \\text{Total Capacity} = 24 \\text{ eggs/tray} \\times 2 \\text{ trays} = 48 \\text{ eggs} $$\n\n**Step 2: Compare the total capacity to the number of eggs Jaime has.**\nJaime has 64 eggs in total.\n$$ \\text{Eggs remaining} = \\text{Total Eggs} - \\text{Total Capacity} $$\n$$ \\text{Eggs remaining} = 64 - 48 $$\n\n**Step 3: Perform the subtraction.**\n$$ 64 - 48 = 16 $$\n\nJaime will have 16 eggs that he cannot place on the trays.\n\n#### 16<|im_end|>",
      "answer_text": "To solve this problem, we need to determine the total capacity of the trays and compare it to the number of eggs Jaime has.\n\n**Step 1: Calculate the total number of eggs the trays can hold.**\nEach tray holds 24 eggs, and Jaime has 2 trays.\n$$ \\text{Total Capacity} = 24 \\text{ eggs/tray} \\times 2 \\text{ trays} = 48 \\text{ eggs} $$\n\n**Step 2: Compare the total capacity to the number of eggs Jaime has.**\nJaime has 64 eggs in total.\n$$ \\text{Eggs remaining} = \\text{Total Eggs} - \\text{Total Capacity} $$\n$$ \\text{Eggs remaining} = 64 - 48 $$\n\n**Step 3: Perform the subtraction.**\n$$ 64 - 48 = 16 $$\n\nJaime will have 16 eggs that he cannot place on the trays.\n\n#### 16",
